# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 007
# Act: INS+  (Instance aimed at Figure)   Stance: Making   Site: Entity
#
# INS's second use: the anchor is actually minted. Computed, not chosen —
# a SHA-256 digest over exactly what turn-5 earned (site-role, sign, kind
# members, negative control), canonically ordered so recomputing it from
# kernel/data/anchor-001.json reproduces the identical digest forever, on
# any engine. This is the whole point of an anchor over a sign: SHA-256 is
# fully specified, not implementation-approximated the way Math.cos/log
# are (see eoreader6's determinism audit, KERNEL_REBUILD_CHECKPOINT.md) —
# an anchor that could differ by host engine would not be an anchor.
#
# Anchor: @444b54f3c0bfb037 (first 16 hex chars; full digest in
# kernel/data/anchor-001.json). This is now the entity's permanent,
# frame-independent identity — "index:16 of 32 - midpoint, absent" as a
# human-readable sign may be renamed later (SIG's naming stays revisable);
# this anchor will not change unless the content it hashes does, and if it
# does, that is a new entity, not a rename of this one.
#
# Earning argument: precondition is turn-6 (INS−, cultivating the ground)
# and, transitively, turn-5's stable sign. Refuted if the digest in
# anchor-001.json does not match SHA-256(content) recomputed independently
# — checkable by anyone, not asserted on trust.

:turn-7  eot:opens        :turn-6 .
:turn-7  eot:act          eot:INS+ .
:turn-7  eot:stance       "Making" .
:turn-7  eot:site         "Entity" .
:turn-7  eot:mints        "@444b54f3c0bfb0371d605a7c0d57698df6f6dc895d2a2941cc550d6ae5546f0d" .
:turn-7  eot:evidence     "kernel/data/anchor-001.json" .
:turn-7  eot:closes       [ eot:aperture 1.0 ; eot:perturbation "none" ] .
